### =================================================================###
### Libreria - Pruebas de los servicios a traves del gateway
### Cliente HTTP de IntelliJ (los scripts "> {% ... %}" guardan el token).
### Docker: gateway en 8762. Local (sin Docker): cambiar @gateway a 8760.
### Documentacion interactiva: {{gateway}}/swagger-ui.html
### =================================================================###
@gateway = http://localhost:8762
@authServer = http://localhost:9000
@clientId = gateway-app
@clientSecret = gateway-secret

### =================================================================###
### 0. Preparacion: registrar un usuario demo (una sola vez).
### Usa un token de aplicacion (client_credentials) solo para esto;
### la clave se cifra en el auth. Si ya existe, omitir.
### =================================================================###
POST {{authServer}}/oauth2/token
Authorization: Basic {{clientId}} {{clientSecret}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials&scope=read write

> {%
    client.global.set("appToken", response.body.access_token);
%}

###
POST {{gateway}}/api/users
Authorization: Bearer {{appToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userName": "demo",
  "password": "demo1234",
  "enabled": true,
  "roles": [ { "id": 1 } ]
}

### =================================================================###
### 1. LOGIN de usuario (via gateway -> auth) -> guarda {{token}}
### =================================================================###
POST {{gateway}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "demo",
  "password": "demo1234"
}

> {%
    client.test("Login correcto", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "Se esperaba 200");
    });
    client.global.set("token", response.body.access_token);
%}

### Login con clave incorrecta (espera 401)
POST {{gateway}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "demo",
  "password": "incorrecta"
}

> {%
    client.test("Credenciales invalidas", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 401, "Se esperaba 401");
    });
%}

### Sin token (espera 401)
GET {{gateway}}/api/books

> {%
    client.test("Sin token no pasa", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 401, "Se esperaba 401");
    });
%}

### LOGOUT: revoca el token actual (204). Despues de esto el token da 401.
### Vuelva a ejecutar el login para obtener uno nuevo.
POST {{gateway}}/api/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

> {%
    client.test("Logout correcto", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 204, "Se esperaba 204");
    });
%}

### Token revocado (espera 401 si se ejecuta justo despues del logout)
GET {{gateway}}/api/books
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### =================================================================###
### 1b. Token de aplicacion (client_credentials) - solo para el cliente,
### no representa a un usuario. Guarda {{token}}.
### =================================================================###
POST {{authServer}}/oauth2/token
Authorization: Basic {{clientId}} {{clientSecret}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials&scope=read write

> {%
    client.test("Token obtenido", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "Se esperaba 200");
    });
    client.global.set("token", response.body.access_token);
%}

### =================================================================###
### 2. LIBROS  (/api/books -> service-books)
### =================================================================###

### Listar libros
GET {{gateway}}/api/books
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Listar libros paginado
GET {{gateway}}/api/books/pagina?page=0&size=5
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Buscar libro por id
GET {{gateway}}/api/books/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Crear libro (categoria 1 = romance, 2 = drama, 3 = comedia)
POST {{gateway}}/api/books
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Cien anos de soledad",
  "subTitle": "Edicion de bolsillo",
  "datePublication": "1967-05-30",
  "price": 45000,
  "categoria": { "id": 1 }
}

> {%
    client.test("Libro creado", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 201, "Se esperaba 201");
    });
    client.global.set("bookId", response.body.isbn);
%}

### Actualizar libro creado (404 si no existe)
PUT {{gateway}}/api/books/{{bookId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Cien anos de soledad (2da edicion)",
  "subTitle": "Tapa dura",
  "datePublication": "1967-05-30",
  "price": 60000,
  "categoria": { "id": 1 }
}

### Eliminar libro creado
DELETE {{gateway}}/api/books/{{bookId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### =================================================================###
### 3. USUARIOS  (/api/users -> service-users)
### Los roles disponibles son 1 = USER, 2 = ADMIN, 3 = PROFESOR
### POST y PUT pasan por el auth, que cifra la clave (BCrypt).
### =================================================================###

### Listar usuarios
GET {{gateway}}/api/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Listar usuarios paginado
GET {{gateway}}/api/users/pagina?page=0&size=5
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Buscar usuario por id
GET {{gateway}}/api/users/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Buscar usuario por nombre de usuario
GET {{gateway}}/api/users/buscar-username?userName=prueba
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Crear usuario (la respuesta trae la clave cifrada)
POST {{gateway}}/api/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userName": "Lucas",
  "password": "lucasFil123",
  "enabled": true,
  "roles": [ { "id": 1 } ]
}

> {%
    client.test("Usuario creado", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 201, "Se esperaba 201");
        client.assert(response.body.password.startsWith("$2"), "La clave debe venir cifrada");
    });
    client.global.set("userId", response.body.id);
%}

### Login con el usuario recien creado
POST {{gateway}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "Lucas",
  "password": "lucasFil123"
}

> {%
    client.test("Login del nuevo usuario", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "Se esperaba 200");
    });
    client.global.set("token", response.body.access_token);
%}

### Actualizar usuario creado (la clave es obligatoria)
PUT {{gateway}}/api/users/{{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userName": "Lucas",
  "password": "lucasFil123",
  "enabled": false,
  "roles": [ { "id": 1 }, { "id": 3 } ]
}

### Eliminar usuario creado
DELETE {{gateway}}/api/users/{{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### =================================================================###
### 4. Documentacion OpenAPI (publica, sin token)
### =================================================================###

### OpenAPI del servicio de libros
GET {{gateway}}/api/books/v3/api-docs

### OpenAPI del servicio de usuarios
GET {{gateway}}/api/users/v3/api-docs
